{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat /work/board.md && ls -l /work'","aggregated_output":"[sol] 2026-10-22: Reading problem; deriving geometric condition for centroid = VCG projection. Will coordinate exact classification and proof here.\n[sol] 2026-10-22: Derived reduction: D=sum(v_i)-v_P, w_i=min(v_i,D). For positive values and v_P>0, equality iff all w_i equal OR every pair w_i+w_j <= D. Proof via y_i=w_i-(v_i-p_i), sum h=sum(w)-D; centroid of triangle sum y=h truncated by y_i<=w_i. Removed corner triangles disjoint since w_i<=D. Centroid at h/3 iff w_i(h-w_i)_+^2 equal. Distinct positive values satisfying this force h=x+z+sqrt(xz), contradict sum w=h+D and w_i<=D. Working edge cases and explicit example.\n[argon] 2026-10-22: Read problem and sol's notes. Writing a Python verification script to check the geometry of F, VCG projection vs centroid, and all boundary/degenerate cases (v_P <= 0, 1D/0D faces, binding caps on p^VCG projection).\n[sol] 2026-10-22: Simplified classification for positive winner values: equality iff all v_A=v_B=v_C OR min(v_i)>=min(v_P, V-v_P). Equivalently v_P<=min(v_i) or v_P>=V-min(v_i), plus equal values. If any winner value is zero, F has <=1 dimension and equality always (two-positive case y segment with sum h<=each positive w cap). Will write detailed proof and example unless argon prefers alternate role.\n[sol] 2026-10-22: Drafted answer.md with complete classification, geometric proof, zero-value cases, and example (v_A,v_B,v_C;v_P)=(1,2,3;3): VN=(1,1,1), centroid=(1/2,1,3/2). Argon: please review independently and run your checks before final designation.\ntotal 16\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent 5210 Oct 22 20:38 answer.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent 1524 Oct 22 20:38 board.md\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 agent agent   70 Oct 22 20:36 logs\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent 2036 Oct 22 20:36 problem.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
